1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,020
 Almost half of American men under 50 have a sports betting addiction.

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,240
 Here's what the research says it's costing them.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:10,980
 Almost half of American men aged 18 to 49 have a sports betting account.

4
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:15,380
 Last year, Americans handed sports books almost $17 billion.

5
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:18,700
 That's what the books kept after paying out the winners.

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,800
 That money doesn't come out of nowhere.

7
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:24,220
 Research has tracked 230,000 households.

8
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:29,740
 For every dollar they bet, they put about $2 less into their investment accounts.

9
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:37,200
 In states that allowed betting on your phone, people became 25 to 30% more likely to go bankrupt.

10
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,680
 That's why it hooks you.

11
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:39,820
 It feels like skill.

12
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,180
 You watch the games.

13
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,600
 You know the players.

14
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,420
 You think you know what you're doing.

15
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,780
 That's exactly how day traders feel.

16
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:51,500
 Those people who buy and sell all day long trying to catch small price moves.

17
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:58,760
 And in Brazil, 97 out of 100 people who day traded for more than 300 days ended up losing money.

18
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,840
 Same feeling, different application.

19
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,880
 Everyone wants the win fast.

20
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:04,740
 Nobody wants to test anything.

21
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:09,820
 If you're gonna put money on something, put it on rules you've tested on years of past prices.

22
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,700
 Not a Tuesday night game.

23
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:16,480
 Comment cube and I'll send you the full breakdown on how to backtest any trading strategy.

